			<title>Beth Ditto performs Madonna's Vogue at NYC Fashion's Night Out</title>
			<link>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/66-beth-ditto-performes-madonnas-vogue-at-nyc-fashions-night-out.html</link>
			<guid>http://www.drownedmadonna.com/index/item/66-beth-ditto-performes-madonnas-vogue-at-nyc-fashions-night-out.html</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="K2FeedIntroText"><p>Last night was a special night in <strong>New York City</strong> and <strong>Milan</strong> for all fashion victims: it was the <strong>Fashion Night Out</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><strong>Gossip</strong>'s frontwoman <strong>Beth Ditto</strong> performed at <strong>M.A.C. Cosmetics store</strong> in <strong>Soho</strong>, <strong>NYC</strong>, to promote her cool <strong>EP</strong>, which is a homage to the 90's. "First of all, house music, especially from the Nineties, is the gayest music ever," she told <strong>Rolling Stone</strong>. "It's all drum and bass, which is perfect for parties."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>During the gig she also she performed <strong>Madonna's Vogue</strong>, "complete with a troupe of gesticulating, eye-liner-laden males writhing behind her," reports the <strong>Rolling Stone</strong>. "The response? Uproarious."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>{youtube}RHCAmhIN7b0{/youtube}</p>
<p> </p>
<p>Last night gig was to promote <strong>Beth Ditto</strong>'s <strong>EP</strong>, whose first single, <strong>I Wrote the Book</strong>, video absolutely has a <strong>Vogue</strong>-ish vibe as well some reference to <strong>Justify My Love</strong>... and we really like it!</p>
<p> </p>
<p>{youtube}UECeJzd-G30{/youtube}</p>
<p> </p>
<p>It was not the first time that <strong>Beth Ditto</strong> enjoyed performing <strong>Vogue</strong>, for instance, she also did it at <strong>London</strong>'s <strong>Lovebox Festival</strong> and in<strong> Moscow</strong>'s<strong> Miller party</strong>.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>So <strong>Beth Ditto</strong> loves <strong>Madonna</strong>. But is the feeling mutual? Reportedly <strong>Madonna</strong> loves <strong>Beth</strong>, and in July <strong>Madonna</strong>'s manager <strong>Guy Oseary</strong> twetted: "I just showed <strong>Madonna</strong> the video of <strong>Beth Ditto</strong> performing <strong>Vogue</strong> at <strong>Moscow Miller party</strong>, She thought Beth was great..."</p>
<p> </p>
<p>{youtube}kA16g7Fvxs0{/youtube}</p></div><div class="K2FeedTags"><ul><li>Vogue</li><ul></div>]]></description>
